 "reference": "Numerics @ 2a0357a. The consumption/income/production/savings/unemployment sample (n=187) is Test_LinearRegression.cs's own R-validated dataset, reused verbatim across its Simple/Multiple/Predict/PredictionIntervals test methods; this file reuses it the same way across cases rather than re-deriving it. `fit`'s per-case tolerances match the C# test's own Assert.AreEqual deltas exactly (loosest for the multi-predictor R-squared/adj-R-squared and the 1E-1 PredictionIntervals checks, tightest for Predict's 1E-6). `residuals`/`covariance` have no direct C# test assertion (LinearRegression's own tests check ParameterStandardErrors and Predict/PredictionIntervals, never Residuals or Covariance directly), so those two cases were curated via `python3 tools/verify_oracles.py --dump` against the real Numerics.Data.LinearRegression, per corehydro CLAUDE.md rule 3/4 (an expected value must come from an upstream C# test file or the emitter's dump mode, never from this repo's own C++).",
